Z||000000||fldevel||07-22-2001||01:58 PM||||ok .. the other day i was sitting in my car after i got back from the gas station listening to music when all of a sudden my car just STALLS it sputteres a bit and than just quit like it ran outa gas .. i tried to restart the car and it started but started choking and died once more ..i tried to re-crank it again and it wouldent do anything .. i checked spark and engine is getting fuel cause it smells flooded.. i let it sit over night and tried to re-start this morining and still nothing .. any info would be greatly appreciated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000001||ichifiero||07-22-2001||02:05 PM||||I am not sure if you are flooding or starving your engine. Have you tried to spray starting fluid in the intake to see if it will fire? The smell of gas could be a leaking fuel line. Just some ideas.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||07-22-2001||02:29 PM||||Sounds electrical. I don't know what engine you have, but I would check: p/up coil, ign module, ign coil. AutoZone can test all 3, but even if it test good, it doesn't guarantee it it. Other than that, plugs, wires, cap, rotor. Make sure the coil wire going to the dist is in good shape and not cooked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jimmy||07-22-2001||02:40 PM||||What motor or fiero do you have?||||reg||1
Z||000004||beachbomb||07-22-2001||02:59 PM||||HI, hope its not what happened to mine, i was going down the interstate and the engine just died, had spark and gas(smelled like it was flooded), i later found out it was my camshaft timing gear(i'm repairing it as we speak), the easy way to see if it is this(which i hope for you its not, what a PAIN!!) open the cap where you put oil in the engine and have someone turn the engine over while you're looking in the hole where the cap goes, if you see NO movement of the valves or anything, then you're timing gear is gone! A repair shop here wanted $1000 to do mine, needless to say its in my garage and i'm doing it, good luck..jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||1
Z||000005||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||03:02 PM||||the same exact thing happened to me and it ended up being my FUEL PUMP.  It cost me around 400 dollars to find the problem and fix it.  i was also driving down the road when my car suddenly stalled. i then tried to restart it and it kicked over for a second and died again.  I would check this.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||07-22-2001||04:00 PM||||I assume since it stumbled after trying to start it, the cam was still spinning as usual, but I might be wrong.<P>Fuel pump is a possibility too. But, I have found everytime the engine will fire for 1-2 seconds before dying, even if the pump is killed completely.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
